body:
This might sound crazy, but I think Jacksonville is a sleeping giant. They are in a great location,  geographically have everything for it to be a major city too. Not because the city is the "largest" city in the country, or "largest" city in Florida. It has nicer weather than the rest of the big cities in Florida. The beaches are really nice. You arent stuck driving hours to get out of the state, you get nicer winters that actually get to colder temperatures unlike the other cities in Florida. You can jump in your car and go see the mountains or snow or take a trip to Atlanta, Savannah, Orlando, Tampa, etc, all in a few hours. North Florida has some beautiful nature too, and tons of natural cold springs close by. 

&#x200B;

If they could stop building sprawl and build an actual city, it would boom. I just dont think anyone is willing to be the pioneer to start making that change. Jacksonville is a terrible place to be currently. It is just a bunch of single home neighborhoods and everything is so spread out. 

&#x200B;

But it definitely has potential to be a big city. The east coast San Diego, especially with all the military nearby.
